te, update, archive, restore, query, search, and manage Notion pages, databases, blocks, users, and comments. The runtime resolves Notion OAuth from Connections and returns raw Notion data under data.","tips":[],"docsHref":"/docs/nodes/notion","why":"Preserves the source Notion template lookup while replacing Typeform Trigger with Form."}}},{"id":"ai_agent","type":"custom","position":{"x":740,"y":300},"data":{"icon":"Bot","type":"ai_agent","label":"AI Agent","category":"ai","config":{"model":"gemini-3.5-flash","temperature":0.2,"userInput":"Process this workflow input and any attached tool results: {{input}}","systemPrompt":"Draft a warm welcome package and first-week checklist for this new hire based on role and team. Return ONLY JSON with the fields named in this workflow.","outputFormat":"json","memoryScope":"none","requireApprovalFor":"destructive"},"notes":{"family":"AI","what":"An autonomous AI brain that reasons, makes decisions, and uses tools on your behalf","overview":"Runs one prompt-driven AI step. The runtime extracts userInput from this node or upstream message-like fields, infers the provider from Model, calls the LLM adapter, and packages response_text plus optional structured fields.","tips":[],"docsHref":"/docs/nodes/ai_agent","why":"Applies the source AI-agent prompt to the current request and attached read-side context, returning structured JSON for deterministic downstream steps."}}},{"id":"js_parse_agent","type":"custom","position":{"x":1060,"y":300},"data":{"icon":"Code","type":"javascript","label":"Parse Agent JSON","category":"data","config":{"code":"const raw = input.response_text || input.output || input.response || input.text || input.content || \"\";\nlet parsed = {};\ntry {\n  const match = String(raw).match(/\\{[\\s\\S]*\\}/);\n  parsed = match ? JSON.parse(match[0]) : {};\n} catch (error) {\n  parsed = {};\n}\nconst message = parsed.message || parsed.reply || parsed.emailBody || parsed.body || parsed.summary || String(raw);\nreturn { ...input, ...parsed, responseText: String(raw), message };","timeout":5000},"notes":{"family":"Data","what":"Writes and runs any JavaScript you like to transform or process your data","overview":"Run sandboxed JavaScript once against the current workflow data and return the transformed value for downstream nodes.","tips":["Always return the value the next node should receive","Default timeout is 5000ms and runtime caps at 30000ms","Use Output Schema such as {\"type\":\"object\"} only as a top-level shape hint","JavaScript has no credentials; connect downstream service node accounts separately","Do not paste API keys, tokens, or passwords into code"],"docsHref":"/docs/nodes/javascript","why":"Turns the agent response into top-level fields before any branch or output node reads it."}}},{"id":"notion_create_onboarding","type":"custom","position":{"x":1380,"y":300},"data":{"icon":"BookOpen","type":"notion","label":"Create Onboarding Page","category":"data","config":{"operation":"create_page","databaseId":"REPLACE_WITH_ONBOARDING_DB","title":"{{input.newHireName}} onboarding","content":"{{input.message}}"},"notes":{"family":"Data","what":"Creates, reads, or updates pages and databases in Notion","overview":"Read, create, update, archive, restore, query, search, and manage Notion pages, databases, blocks, users, and comments. The runtime resolves Notion OAuth from Connections and returns raw Notion data under data.","tips":[],"docsHref":"/docs/nodes/notion","why":"Creates the onboarding page as the durable workspace for the new hire."}}},{"id":"gmail_welcome_hire","type":"custom","position":{"x":1700,"y":300},"data":{"icon":"Mail","type":"google_gmail","label":"Email New Hire","category":"output","config":{"operation":"send","recipientSource":"manual_entry","recipientEmails":"{{input.newHireEmail}}","subject":"Welcome to the team","body":"{{input.message}}"},"notes":{"family":"Communication","what":"Send emails from your Gmail account or read and search messages in your inbox","overview":"Send, list, get, or search Gmail messages. Send recipients can be typed manually or extracted from upstream/fallback Google Sheets rows.","tips":["Connect Google OAuth in Connections; do not paste tokens into workflow fields","Gmail search syntax: from:, subject:, is:unread, has:attachment","List/Search only return {id, threadId} per message â€” use a Get step with that id for full content","Body is plain text only","Get returns Gmail's raw API message; the body text is base64url-encoded inside message.payload.body.data","Use search to filter messages before getting details"],"docsHref":"/docs/nodes/google_gmail","why":"Sends the welcome package to the new hire."}}},{"id":"slack_new_hire","type":"custom","position":{"x":2020,"y":300},"data":{"icon":"Hash","type":"slack_message","label":"Notify People Ops","category":"output","config":{"channel":"#new-hires","message":"New hire onboarding created for {{input.newHireName}}"},"notes":{"family":"Communication","what":"Sends messages using a Slack app or bot connection","overview":"Send Slack bot messages to channels, direct messages, or existing threads through a saved Slack OAuth2 connection. Use it for workplace alerts, support replies, incident updates, approvals, report summaries, and deployment notifications.","tips":["Select a Slack OAuth2 connection; do not paste bot tokens into message fields","The Slack app needs chat:write, and the bot must be invited before it can post in private channels","Use {{$json.channelId}} and {{$json.threadTs}} from Slack Trigger to reply in the same conversation","Keep Message filled as readable fallback text even when Blocks contains a rich Block Kit layout","Connect downstream service accounts separately; Slack OAuth2 only authorizes the Slack send"],"docsHref":"/docs/nodes/slack_message","why":"Notifies the team that onboarding has started."}}}]$tpl$::jsonb,
